{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of distinct lines representing the altitudes, medians, and interior angle bisectors of a triangle that is isosceles, but not equilateral, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0f86ec456819d72489b08f1a17bce7c08383bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 7\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 5\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c074d10f96a6f5c980cab1ed2ca66f23702c8cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(2cm); draw((-3,0)--(0,4)--(3,0)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(0,4), red);  draw((-3,0)--(0.84, 2.88), green); draw((-3,0)--(1.5, 2), green); draw((-3,0)--(1.636, 1.818), green);  draw((3,0)--(-0.84, 2.88), blue); draw((3,0)--(-1.5, 2), blue); draw((3,0)--(-1.636, 1.818), blue); [/asy]\" width=\"95\" height=\"65\" />\n</p><p>As shown in the diagram above, all nine altitudes, medians, and interior angle bisectors are distinct, except for the three coinciding lines from the vertex opposite to the base. Thusly, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct lines, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />, and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1957 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1957\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\"